# Development

Initialize with `go mod init {{project_slug}}`, then resolve the test dependency:

```sh
go get github.com/stretchr/testify
go mod tidy
make install
```

If the project chooses a remote module path, change it with `go mod edit
-module <path>` and replace `{{project_slug}}/internal/` imports in every Go
file. Install golangci-lint using its official instructions, and write its
installed version to `.golangci-lint-version`. The config's version key is
the config format, not a pinned tool release. Keep its linters when adapting
the config to a new release.

```sh
make fmt-check vet lint build test test-integration
go test -race -run TestRequestFailures ./internal/httpapi/
make coverage
```

Unit and handler tests run with the race detector; it requires cgo and a C
compiler. Tagged integration tests also build the server with `-race`.
TestMain builds once into a temporary directory. Each test starts the binary
with PORT=0, reads the actual address from JSON logs, keeps draining stdout
and kills any surviving child in cleanup. Signal cases check both SIGINT and
SIGTERM, exit status and the final stopped record.

`make fmt` applies gofmt and goimports. `make serve` builds `bin/server`,
embeds version metadata and runs it in the foreground. `make ci` adds coverage
and vulnerability checks. A standard-library advisory needs a patched Go
toolchain, recorded in go.mod, rather than a disabled vulnerability check.

Fill README and the selected fragments' AGENTS, hook and CI guidance before
the final `stacks verify`. The default hooks and workflow are supplied by
their fragments; this slice does not write their files.
